"<div>\n<i class=\"NoteType\">\nCitation\n</i>\n<div class=\"grampsstylednote\">\n<p>\nSource Citation<br />\nYear: 1910; Census Place: Yount, Napa, California; Roll: T624_90; Page: 11a; Enumeration District: 0085; FHL microfilm: 1374103\n</p>\n<p>\nDescription<br />\nEnumeration District: 0085; Description: Yount Township (part), excluding Veterans Home of California, Rutherford Precinct, Yount Precinct\n</p>\n<p>\nSource Information<br />\nAncestry.com. 1910 United States Federal Census [database on-line]. Lehi, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2006.<br />\nOriginal data:Thirteenth Census of the United States, 1910 (NARA microfilm publication T624, 1,178 rolls). Records of the Bureau of the Census, Record Group 29. National Archives, Washington, D.C. For details on the contents of the film numbers, visit the following NARA web page: NARA.\n</p>\n<p>\nSource Description<br />\nThis database is an index to the head of households enumerated in the 1910 United States Federal Census, the Thirteenth Census of the United States. In addition, each indexed name is linked to actual images of the 1910 Federal Census. The information recorded in the census includes: name, relationship to head of family, age at last birthday, sex, color or race, whether single, married, widowed, or divorced, birthplace, birthplace of father and mother, and more.\n</p>\n<p>\n&nbsp;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
"<div>\n<i class=\"NoteType\">\nCitation\n</i>\n<div class=\"grampsstylednote\">\n<p>\nSource Citation<br />\nYear: 1920; Census Place: Civil District 2, Grundy, Tennessee; Roll: T625_1741; Page: 10A; Enumeration District: 38\n</p>\n<p>\nDescription<br />\nEnumeration District: 0038; Description: Civil District 2 (part) excluding Altamont town including Almshouse, all that part of the 2nd Civil District lying to the eastward of a line beginning on the 8th District line at headwaters of Collins River, running up Big Creek to Altamont and Coalmont and Coalmont Rd, thence with this road to Coalmont Depot, thence with Tracy City Railroad to the line of the 5th Civil District\n</p>\n<p>\nSource Information<br />\nAncestry.com. 1920 United States Federal Census [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations, Inc., 2010. Images reproduced by FamilySearch.<br />\nOriginal data:Fourteenth Census of the United States, 1920. (NARA microfilm publication T625, 2076 rolls). Records of the Bureau of the Census, Record Group 29. National Archives, Washington, D.C. For details on the contents of the film numbers, visit the following NARA web page: NARA. Note: Enumeration Districts 819-839 are on roll 323 (Chicago City).\n</p>\n<p>\nSource Description<br />\nThis database is an index to individuals enumerated in the 1920 United States Federal Census, the Fourteenth Census of the United States. It includes all states and territories, as well as Military and Naval Forces, the Virgin Islands, Puerto Rico, American Samoa, Guam, and the Panama Canal Zone. The census provides many details about individuals and families including: name, gender, age, birthplace, year of immigration, mother tongue, and parents\u2019 birthplaces. In addition, the names of those listed on the population schedule are linked to actual images of the 1920 Federal Census.\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
"<div>\n<i class=\"NoteType\">\nCitation\n</i>\n<div class=\"grampsstylednote\">\n<p>\nSource Citation<br />\nYear: 1920; Census Place: Pipestone, Pipestone, Minnesota; Roll: T625_850; Page: 10A; Enumeration District: 178\n</p>\n<p>\nDescription<br />\nEnumeration District: 0178; Description: Pipestone City (part), Ward 1 including Pipestone County Jail but excluding Pipestone Indian School, all west of Hiawatha\n</p>\n<p>\nSource Information<br />\nAncestry.com. 1920 United States Federal Census [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations, Inc., 2010. Images reproduced by FamilySearch.<br />\nOriginal data:Fourteenth Census of the United States, 1920. (NARA microfilm publication T625, 2076 rolls). Records of the Bureau of the Census, Record Group 29. National Archives, Washington, D.C. For details on the contents of the film numbers, visit the following NARA web page: NARA. Note: Enumeration Districts 819-839 are on roll 323 (Chicago City).\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
